\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesu, Thy boundless love to me
\par No thought can reach, no tongue declare,
\par O knit my thankful heart to Thee,
\par And reign without a rival there:
\par Thine wholly, Thine alone, I am,
\par Be Thou alone my constant flame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O grant that nothing in my soul
\par May dwell but Thy pure love alone;
\par O may Thy love possess me whole,
\par My joy, my treasure, and my crown
\par Strange flames far from my heart remove,
\par My every act, word, thought, be love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Love, how cheering is Thy ray;
\par All pain before Thy presence flies,
\par Care, anguish, sorrow, melt away,
\par Where'er Thy healing beams arise:
\par O Jesu, nothing  may I see,
\par Nothing desire, or seek, but Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Unwearled may I this pursue,
\par Dauntless to the high prize aspire,
\par Hourly within my soul renew
\par This holy flame this heavenly fire
\par And day and night be all my care
\par To guard the sacred treasure there.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

